I think I have to agree with lorxus. The term {silna} is underdocumented.
In chemical sense different salts can elicit all five basic tastes, e.g.,
salty (sodium chloride), sweet (lead diacetate, which will cause lead
poisoning if ingested), sour (potassium bitartrate), bitter (magnesium
sulfate), and umami or savory (monosodium glutamate).
[1]<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_(chemistry)#Taste>

So I suggest that {silna} is reserved for NaCl and for salts in general we
choose another term.





